<section>
  <exercises>
    <heading level="1">Section 3.4 Exercises</heading>
    <paragraph>Express the rational function as a sum or difference of two simpler rational expressions.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="182" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{x^{2} + 3x + 1}{(x + 2){(x - 3)}^{2}{(x^{2} + 4)}^{2}}dx.}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="183" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{1}{(x - 3)(x - 2)}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- 2 x + 1 + 5 2 ( x + 2 ) + 1 2 x - 2 x + 1 + 5 2 ( x + 2 ) + 1 2 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="184" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{x^{2} + 1}{x(x + 1)(x + 2)}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="185" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{1}{x^{3} - x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 x 2 + 3 x 1 x 2 + 3 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="186" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{3x + 1}{x^{2}}$$ (Hint: Use long division first.)</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="187" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{3x^{2}}{x^{2} + 1}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 x 2 + 4 x + 8 + 16 x - 2 2 x 2 + 4 x + 8 + 16 x - 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="188" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{2x^{4}}{x^{2} - 2x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="189" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{1}{(x - 1)(x^{2} + 1)}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- 1 x 2 - 1 x + 1 x - 1 - 1 x 2 - 1 x + 1 x - 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="190" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{1}{x^{2}(x - 1)}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="191" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{x}{x^{2} - 4}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- 1 2 ( x - 2 ) + 1 2 ( x - 1 ) - 1 6 x + 1 6 ( x - 3 ) - 1 2 ( x - 2 ) + 1 2 ( x - 1 ) - 1 6 x + 1 6 ( x - 3 )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="192" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{1}{x(x - 1)(x - 2)(x - 3)}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="193" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{1}{x^{4} - 1} = \frac{1}{(x + 1)(x - 1)\left( {x^{2} + 1} \right)}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 x - 1 + 2 x + 1 x 2 + x + 1 1 x - 1 + 2 x + 1 x 2 + x + 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="194" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{3x^{2}}{x^{3} - 1} = \frac{3x^{2}}{(x - 1)(x^{2} + x + 1)}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="195" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{2x}{{(x + 2)}^{2}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 x + 1 + x x 2 + 4 - 1 ( x 2 + 4 ) 2 2 x + 1 + x x 2 + 4 - 1 ( x 2 + 4 ) 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Use the method of partial fractions to evaluate each of the following integrals.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="196" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{3x^{4} + x^{3} + 20x^{2} + 3x + 31}{(x + 1)\left( {x^{2} + 4} \right)^{2}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="197" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int\frac{dx}{(x - 3)(x - 2)}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$ln | x - 2 | + 2 ln | x + 4 | + C ln | x - 2 | + 2 ln | x + 4 | + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="198" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{3x}{x^{2} + 2x - 8}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="199" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int\frac{dx}{x^{3} - x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 2 ln | 4 - x 2 | + C 1 2 ln | 4 - x 2 | + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="200" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{x}{x^{2} - 4}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="201" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int\frac{dx}{x(x - 1)(x - 2)(x - 3)}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 ( x + 1 3 arctan ( 1 + x 3 ) ) + C 2 ( x + 1 3 arctan ( 1 + x 3 ) ) + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="202" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{2x^{2} + 4x + 22}{x^{2} + 2x + 10}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="203" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int\frac{dx}{x^{2} - 5x + 6}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 ln | x | - 3 ln | 1 + x | + C 2 ln | x | - 3 ln | 1 + x | + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="204" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{2 - x}{x^{2} + x}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="205" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{2}{x^{2} - x - 6}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 16 ( - 4 -2 + x - ln | -2 + x | + ln | 2 + x | ) + C 1 16 ( - 4 -2 + x - ln | -2 + x | + ln | 2 + x | ) + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="206" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int\frac{dx}{x^{3} - 2x^{2} - 4x + 8}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Evaluate the following integrals, which have irreducible quadratic factors.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="207" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int\frac{dx}{x^{4} - 10x^{2} + 9}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 30 ( -2 5 arctan [ 1 + x 5 ] + 2 ln | -4 + x | - ln | 6 + 2 x + x 2 | ) + C 1 30 ( -2 5 arctan [ 1 + x 5 ] + 2 ln | -4 + x | - ln | 6 + 2 x + x 2 | ) + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="208" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{2}{(x - 4)\left( {x^{2} + 2x + 6} \right)}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="209" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{x^{2}}{x^{3} - x^{2} + 4x - 4}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- 3 x + 4 ln | x + 2 | + x + C - 3 x + 4 ln | x + 2 | + x + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="210" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{x^{3} + 6x^{2} + 3x + 6}{x^{3} + 2x^{2}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Use the method of partial fractions to evaluate the following integrals.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="211" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{x}{(x - 1)\left( {x^{2} + 2x + 2} \right)^{2}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- ln | 3 - x | + 1 2 ln | x 2 + 4 | + C - ln | 3 - x | + 1 2 ln | x 2 + 4 | + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="212" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{3x + 4}{\left( {x^{2} + 4} \right)(3 - x)}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="213" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{2}{{(x + 2)}^{2}(2 - x)}dx}$$ (Hint: Use the rational root theorem.)</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$ln | x - 2 | - 1 2 ln | x 2 + 2 x + 2 | + C ln | x - 2 | - 1 2 ln | x 2 + 2 x + 2 | + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Use substitution to convert the integrals to integrals of rational functions. Then use partial fractions to evaluate the integrals.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="214" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{3x + 4}{x^{3} - 2x - 4}dx}$$ (Give the exact answer and the decimal equivalent. Round to five decimal places.)</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="215" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int_{0}^{1}{\frac{e^{x}}{36 - e^{2x}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$- x + ln | 1 - e x | + C - x + ln | 1 - e x | + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="216" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{e^{x}}{e^{2x} - e^{x}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="217" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int\frac{\sin x dx}{1 - \cos^{2}x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 5 ln | cos x + 3 cos x - 2 | + C 1 5 ln | cos x + 3 cos x - 2 | + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="218" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{\sin x}{\cos^{2}x + \cos x - 6}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="219" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{1 - \sqrt{x}}{1 + \sqrt{x}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 2 - 2 e 2 t + C 1 2 - 2 e 2 t + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="220" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int\frac{dt}{\left( {e^{t} - e^{-t}} \right)^{2}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="221" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{1 + e^{x}}{1 - e^{x}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>24.6 m3</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="222" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int\frac{dx}{1 + \sqrt{x + 1}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="223" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int\frac{dx}{\sqrt{x} + \sqrt[4]{x}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$ln | sin x 1 - sin x | + C ln | sin x 1 - sin x | + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="224" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{\cos x}{\sin x(1 - \sin x)}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="225" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{e^{x}}{\left( {e^{2x} - 4} \right)^{2}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$3 4 3 4$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="226" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int\limits_{1}^{2}{\frac{1}{x^{2}\sqrt{4 - x^{2}}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="227" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{1}{2 + e^{-x}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x - ln ( 1 + e x ) + C x - ln ( 1 + e x ) + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Use the given substitution to convert the integral to an integral of a rational function, then evaluate.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="228" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\int{\frac{1}{1 + e^{x}}dx}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="229" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$${\int{\frac{1}{t - \sqrt[3]{t}}dt}} t = x^{3}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$6 x 1 / 6 - 3 x 1 / 3 + 2 x - 6 ln ( 1 + x 1 / 6 ) + C 6 x 1 / 6 - 3 x 1 / 3 + 2 x - 6 ln ( 1 + x 1 / 6 ) + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="230" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Graph the curve $${\int{\frac{1}{\sqrt{x} + \sqrt[3]{x}}dx}};x = u^{6}$$ over the interval $$y = \frac{x}{1 + x}$$ Then, find the area of the region bounded by the curve, the x-axis, and the line $$\left\lbrack {0,5} \right\rbrack.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="231" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the volume of the solid generated when the region bounded by $$x = 4.$$ $$y = 1/\sqrt{x(3 - x)},$$ $$y = 0,$$ and $$x = 1,$$ is revolved about the x-axis.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$4 3 \pi arctanh [ 1 3 ] = 1 3 \pi ln 4 4 3 \pi arctanh [ 1 3 ] = 1 3 \pi ln 4$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="232" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>The velocity of a particle moving along a line is a function of time given by $$x = 2$$ Find the distance that the particle has traveled after $$v(t) = \frac{88t^{2}}{t^{2} + 1}.$$ sec.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Solve the initial-value problem for x as a function of t.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="233" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$t = 5$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x = - ln | t - 3 | + ln | t - 4 | + ln 2 x = - ln | t - 3 | + ln | t - 4 | + ln 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="234" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {t^{2} - 7t + 12} \right)\frac{dx}{dt} = 1,\left( {t &gt; 4,x(5) = 0} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="235" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$(t + 5)\frac{dx}{dt} = x^{2} + 1,t &gt; -5,x(1) = \tan 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$x = ln | t - 1 | - 2 arctan ( 2 t ) - 1 2 ln ( t 2 + 1 2 ) + 2 arctan ( 2 2 ) + 1 2 ln 4.5 x = ln | t - 1 | - 2 arctan ( 2 t ) - 1 2 ln ( t 2 + 1 2 ) + 2 arctan ( 2 2 ) + 1 2 ln 4.5$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="236" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the x-coordinate of the centroid of the area bounded by</paragraph>
        <paragraph>$$\left( {2t^{3} - 2t^{2} + t - 1} \right)\frac{dx}{dt} = 3,x(2) = 0$$ $$y\left( {x^{2} - 9} \right) = 1,$$ (Round the answer to two decimal places.)</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="237" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the volume generated by revolving the area bounded by $$y = 0,x = 4, \text{and} x = 5.$$ about the y-axis.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 5 \pi ln 28 13 2 5 \pi ln 28 13$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="238" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the area bounded by $$y = \frac{1}{x^{3} + 7x^{2} + 6x}, x = 1,x = 7, \text{and} y = 0$$ $$y = \frac{x - 12}{x^{2} - 8x - 20},$$ (Round the answer to the nearest hundredth.)</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="239" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Evaluate the integral $$y = 0,x = 2, \text{and} x = 4.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$arctan [ -1 + 2 x 3 ] 3 + 1 3 ln | 1 + x | - 1 6 ln | 1 - x + x 2 | + C arctan [ -1 + 2 x 3 ] 3 + 1 3 ln | 1 + x | - 1 6 ln | 1 - x + x 2 | + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following problems, use the substitutions $$\int{\frac{dx}{x^{3} + 1}.}$$ $$\tan \left( \frac{x}{2} \right) = t,$$ $$dx = \frac{2}{1 + t^{2}}dt,$$ and $$\sin x = \frac{2t}{1 + t^{2}},$$</paragraph>
    <exercise number="240" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\cos x = \frac{1 - t^{2}}{1 + t^{2}}.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="241" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Find the area under the curve $$\int\frac{dx}{3 - 5\sin x}$$ between $$y = \frac{1}{1 + \sin x}$$ and $$x = 0$$ (Assume the dimensions are in inches.)</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>2.0 in.2</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="242" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Given $$x = \pi.$$ derive the formulas $$\tan \left( \frac{x}{2} \right) = t,$$ $$dx = \frac{2}{1 + t^{2}}dt,$$ and $$\sin x = \frac{2t}{1 + t^{2}},$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="243" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Evaluate $$\cos x = \frac{1 - t^{2}}{1 + t^{2}}.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$3 ( -8 + x ) 1 / 3 3 ( -8 + x ) 1 / 3$$ $$-2 3 arctan [ -1 + ( -8 + x ) 1 / 3 3 ] -2 3 arctan [ -1 + ( -8 + x ) 1 / 3 3 ]$$ $$-2 ln [ 2 + ( -8 + x ) 1 / 3 ] -2 ln [ 2 + ( -8 + x ) 1 / 3 ]$$ $$+ ln [ 4 - 2 ( -8 + x ) 1 / 3 + ( -8 + x ) 2 / 3 ] + C + ln [ 4 - 2 ( -8 + x ) 1 / 3 + ( -8 + x ) 2 / 3 ] + C$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
  </exercises>
</section>
